  "body": "Follow-up from the review of PR #3125 (#3084), comment 7060737872.\n\nThe posed first-traverse law of PR #3125 reads the work through every pose of the work-turning rotaries. It takes each rotary line through the WCS origin, the same premise as the index-swing clause (`crates/app/src/posting_index_swing.rs` lines 28-40).\n\nA machine file can state a `pivot` or an `offset` for a rotary. No shipped machine file does this, but a user file can. Then the line does not pass through the WCS origin, and the law reads the swept set about the wrong line. The reading can be too low, and the post is not blocked.\n\nWork:\n1. When a work-turning rotary states a non-zero `pivot` or `offset`, read the swept set about the stated line, or refuse the operation by name.\n2. Apply the same rule to the index-swing clause.\n3. Add pinning tests for a machine with an offset rotary line: one refused case and one clear case.\n",
